@startuml startup-activity
skinparam defaultFontName "Noto Sans"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
title Start-up: what F1R3Gaze does to its files before the window opens

start
:**1. Locate** the five roots
--profile, F1R3GAZE_PROFILE, or the platform's folders; <<#DDEBF7>>
:**2. Lock** the anchor <data>/instance.lock,
then <runtime>/instance.lock
(new folders synced in their parents); <<#DDEBF7>>
if (the profile can be written?) then (yes)
  if (the marker names a newer layout?) then (yes)
    :read only, with no busy flag:
    nothing is written to a newer profile; <<#F8CBAD>>
  else (no)
    if (busy flag there, or no marker?) then (yes: the last start did not finish)
      :**3. Barrier**: sync every folder start-up writes into:
      the skeleton, the roots' ancestors, the backups,
      link targets' folders, the migration's plan; <<#FCE4D6>>
    else (no)
      :no barrier: the last start left nothing pending; <<#EDEDED>>
    endif
    :set the busy flag data/.startup-busy
    (not synced: a power cut leaves nothing pending); <<#FFF2CC>>
    :**4. Migrate** an old single-folder profile,
    or create the marker of a new one; <<#DDEBF7>>
    if (the move stopped, or waits?) then (yes)
      :read only from here; the busy flag stays,
      so the next start runs the barrier and resumes; <<#F8CBAD>>
    else (no)
    endif
  endif
else (no: another F1R3Gaze holds it, or it cannot be locked)
  :every step below only reports
  what it would write; <<#EDEDED>>
endif
:**5. Prepare**: create missing skeleton folders,
each synced in its parent, and remove dead writers'
temporary files (never in wallet/keys); <<#DDEBF7>>
if (a folder cannot be made?) then (yes)
  :read only from here; the busy flag stays; <<#F8CBAD>>
else (no)
endif
:**6. Reconcile** each managed file
(see managed-file-states),
then report the wallet keys, which are never written; <<#DDEBF7>>
if (this start set the busy flag, and still writes?) then (yes)
  :**7. Finish**: remove the busy flag,
  sync the data folder: nothing is left pending; <<#FCE4D6>>
else (no)
endif
:**8. Load** the layered settings and
**9. open** the engine, showing what start-up reported; <<#DDEBF7>>
stop

note right
  Steps 3 to 7 are one function, profile::start_up:
  Profile::open, profile check and the trace checks
  all run this one copy of the order.

  **A crash at any step** (a kill, a panic, a power cut):
  the next start finds the busy flag, or no marker,
  and runs the barrier before it decides anything.
  Every write above leaves the old content or the new,
  never a mix, and never nothing where something was.
end note

legend right
  |= Colour |= Meaning |
  |<#DDEBF7> | F1R3Gaze code |
  |<#FFF2CC> | a change not yet durable |
  |<#FCE4D6> | a durability point |
  |<#F8CBAD> | the session goes read-only |
  |<#EDEDED> | a check, or nothing to do |
endlegend
@enduml
